Strata packaged mode: run setup.py and serve/server.py from a read-only tree.

Opt-in: STRATA_STATE_DIR=<writable folder> turns it on; unset, both behave as v0.1.45.
setup.py: configs and settings.json in STRATA_STATE_DIR, data folder STRATA_STATE_DIR/data, no scan for
other Strata folders, no pip, no engine download or compile (engine/strata plus engine/BUILD.json, with a
rebuild hint on a GPU or CPU mismatch), no run script, no log file, port 8095 for a new install, and a stop
(not a fallback into the read-only tree) when the data folder cannot be made.
serve/server.py: a python3 shebang, the config's "port" when no --port is given, an engine with no "log" inherits stderr.
Tests: tools/test_setup_packaged.py, serve/test_packaged.py; tools/test_setup_golden.py names the vision exe <VEXE>
as it names the engine <EXE>, so the golden (recorded on Windows) holds on Linux too.  Not sent upstream.
